    @tableofcontents

    @section pythonintro python Module Introduction

    The \c python module allows for transparent and dynamic bidirectional importing of code from %Qore to %Python and
    vice-versa.  Qore classes can inherit %Python classes and extend them, and %Python classes can inherit %Qore classes
    and extend them as well; even %Qore abstract classes can be inherited by %Python classes and made concrete by
    implementing the required concrete methods in %Python.

    This module also implements support in the same shared object for the \c qoreloader module for %Python so allow
    native %Python code to import %Qore APIs; see @ref python_qoreloader_moduleguide for more information.

    This module is released under LGPL 2.1 or later (see \c COPYING.LGPL in the source distribution).
    Supporting files with MIT notices retain those permissions; bundled CPython internal definitions also
    retain Python's license (see \c COPYING.Python). The module reports its LGPL license to the %Qore runtime.

    To use the module in a %Qore script, use the \c %%requires directive as follows:
    @code{.py} %requires python @endcode

    Helper %Qore classes provided by this module:
    |!Class|!Description
    |@ref Python::PythonProgram "PythonProgram"|Allows %Python code to be embedded and executed in %Qore

    @section python_restrictions Restrictions and Sandboxing

    %Python code is not subject to the restrictions of %Qore @ref Qore::Program "Program" objects (parse options such
    as @ref Qore::PO_NO_FILESYSTEM "PO_NO_FILESYSTEM" or @ref Qore::PO_NO_NETWORK "PO_NO_NETWORK") or to their
    sandbox: it can use the filesystem, start processes and use the network through %Python's own library.  Every way
    to reach %Python from %Qore is therefore an uncontrolled API:
    - the @ref Python::PythonProgram "PythonProgram" class, the %Python classes, methods and functions that the module
      imports into %Qore, and the \c python module commands (\c %%module-cmd(python) and
      @ref Qore::Program::issueModuleCmd() "Program::issueModuleCmd()") cannot be used in a %Program restricted with
      @ref Qore::PO_NO_UNCONTROLLED_APIS "PO_NO_UNCONTROLLED_APIS", which is included in
      @ref Qore::PO_NO_EXTERNAL_ACCESS "PO_NO_EXTERNAL_ACCESS", @ref Qore::PO_NO_IO "PO_NO_IO" and
      @ref Qore::PO_LOCKDOWN "PO_LOCKDOWN"
    - the @ref Python::PythonProgram "PythonProgram" class and the \c parse module command, which parse %Python code at
      runtime, cannot be used in a %Program restricted with @ref Qore::PO_NO_EMBEDDED_LOGIC "PO_NO_EMBEDDED_LOGIC"

    These restrictions also apply to a %Program that inherits the module from its parent %Program without loading it.
    To keep code from running %Python, restrict its %Program with
    @ref Qore::PO_NO_UNCONTROLLED_APIS "PO_NO_UNCONTROLLED_APIS".

    %Qore APIs called from %Python remain subject to the restrictions and the sandbox of the %Program whose %Python
    code calls them, also on threads created by %Python (see @ref python_created_threads).

